[] Here's a question for all you veteran demigods in the audience: when you
[] get a wish, what do you wish for? ...

[hairston@henry.ECE.CMU.EDU (David Hairston) writes:]
[] my 1st wish invariably is: a blessed +3 gray dragon scale mail

[pullen@badger.cs.washington.edu (Walter D. Pullen) writes:]
[] I never wish for dragon scale mail, because the armor will
[] periodically polymorph you into that color of dragon, causing you tear
[] out of your cloak (and hawiian shirt if you have one), so in other
[] words, combining a cloak of magic resistance with other armor will
[] yield a higher AC then gray dragon scale mail.

without the above paragraph, this would have been great advice
(although, as you say, some things could be debated).

the fact of the matter is that dragon scale mail will never
randomly polymorph you.  walking over a polymorph trap will
do that unless you're wearing magic resistant armor (i.e.
gray dragon scale mail).  since dragon scale mail is difficult
to come by, the game seems to take draconian measures to keep
you from losing it because of a self-polymorph.  hence, you
become a dragon of the type of armor you're wearing.  keep
in mind that gray dragon scale mail will prevent that from
happening altogether (in the case of polymorph traps).  IMO,
for the reasons you touched upon, gray dragon scale mail is
the only dragon scale mail worth wearing and when coupled
with a cloak of protection, the AC benefit far outweighs any
other combination of armor and cloak.

as i said at the outset, the rest was A1 advice (altho debatable).

